; Minimal structured-control-flow constructs for the fixture program.
;
; ORIGINAL TEST SOURCE. Not HLL65F, and nothing here is copied from the game
; corpus; these define macros of the same names so the emitter's structured
; lowering can be exercised with no corpus present.
;
; The real package resolves its branch targets by back-patching -- LOC pushes
; the location, FND rewinds and overwrites the placeholder operand once the
; block's length is known. Reproducing that is not the point here, so these
; take the target as an argument instead. What matters to the emitter is
; unchanged: the construct is a macro of this name, and the branch it emits is
; the next instruction.
;
; Note the inversion, which is HLL65F's too: IFEQ emits BNE, because the branch
; jumps *over* the block when the condition does not hold.

	.MACRO IFEQ SKIP
	BNE SKIP
	.ENDM

	.MACRO ENDIF
	.ENDM

	.MACRO BEGIN
	.ENDM

; Note the inversion here too: EQEND names the condition that ENDS the loop, and
; emits the inverse branch back to the top. dialect.md records the real
; package's `BEGIN … PLEND` assembling to `BMI -3`.
	.MACRO EQEND TOP
	BNE TOP
	.ENDM
